        "title": "Find a sum or difference",
        "text": "How is $$\\frac{5\\pi}{12}$$ related to $$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$$ and $$\\frac{\\pi}{4}?$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h2",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h1"
        ],
        "title": "Relate to known angles",
        "text": "Note that $$\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}=\\frac{2\\pi}{12}+\\frac{3\\pi}{12}=\\frac{5\\pi}{12}.$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h3",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h2"
        ],
        "title": "Substitute",
        "text": "$$\\tan\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right)=\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h4",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h3"
        ],
        "title": "Angle sum formula",
        "text": "Recall that $$\\tan(a+b)=\\frac{\\tan(a)+\\tan(b)}{1-\\tan(a)\\tan(b)}$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h5",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h4"
        ],
        "title": "Apply the angle sum formula",
        "text": "$$\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)}{1-\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)}$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h6",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "a6cf981T222-identanglesum-P13a-h5"
        ],
        "title": "Substitute known special values",
        "text": "$$\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}+1}{1-\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)(1)}.$$ Multiplying the top and bottom fractions by $$\\sqrt{3}$$ to clear the nested denominators gives $$\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}-1}.$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
